;; The module _tracemalloc (queue 220; Modules/_tracemalloc.c, Modules/clinic/_tracemalloc.c.h and Python/tracemalloc.c
;; of CPython 3.14.10, PSF License Agreement), its second stage (the user's (a) on 220's DECISION, 2026-11-06). pyi
;; allocates through Go: there is no allocator to hook. An allocation is decided as the creation of a Python object at
;; the runtime's constructors (tmAlloc's callers: NewBytes, NewStr, NewTuple, NewList, NewDict, a frame's cells), its
;; size CPython's for that object as sys.getsizeof gives it (cpythonSizeof; a dict 64, a cell 40), its traceback the running thread's frames, most recent first, the first nframe of them (a frame not
;; yet entered is not on the chain: a callee's cells are its caller's, CPython's "no incomplete frames"). A free is the
;; object's collection, seen by a finalizer (runtime.SetFinalizer) the collector runs; get_traced_memory, _get_traces and
;; take_snapshot collect first and wait for the cleanups, so a dropped object's size is gone when they look, as
;; CPython's refcount frees it at once. Interned tracebacks: one tuple per distinct traceback (the traces share it).
;;
;; What cannot match: CPython's internal allocations (frames, code, the interpreter's buffers, its free lists, the
;; small-int cache, a list's or dict's growth by realloc) are not Python objects made here, so totals and the count of
;; traces differ; a built-in's own Go buffers are none of tracemalloc's. Off, a constructor pays one load of tmOn.

